// A declaration's head is a path into the document's tree. `::field.author(...)`
// is the `author` entry of `::field`, and it is the same entry as
// `::field(author: { ... })` grouped under the name. A trailing `[...]` is the
// entry's prose, and the one positional argument of an entry is the entry
// itself (`::macro.copyright("...")` is `copyright: "..."`). What takes
// several positional arguments, or a file as one, is in `declaration-paths-positional.tmt`.

::kind(fixture)
::id(declaration-paths)

::macro.copyright("(C) 2026 Tomet Projects")
::macro.generated_by[ @comment[ Generated from ${1}. ] ]

::format.meta(always_newline: true)
::format.table(adjust_width: auto, max_col_width: 50)

::field.aliases(type: list, always_newline: true)
::field.url.wiki(type: list, always_newline: true)
